title: Defencism or Internationalism
subtitle: Move the party's line on the war.
new-page: true
is-card: true
tags: party_affairs
view-if: ideology_timer <= 0
on-arrival: month_actions += 1; ideology_timer = 4

The party has no single line. The Revolutionary Defencists want to defend the revolution against the Kaiser and keep the alliance with the liberals. The Internationalists want an immediate general peace and a government of the socialists alone. [? if at_war = 0 : The war with Germany is over; the question is now how to treat the Bolshevik state. ?]

- @defencist: Move toward the Defencists.
- @intl: Move toward the Internationalists.
- @balance: Hold the middle and calm both wings.
- @easy_discard

@defencist
on-arrival: {!
RO.fac(Q, 'defencist', 5, 0);
RO.fac(Q, 'rightdef', 2, -2);
RO.fac(Q, 'intl', -3, 6);
Q.war_line += 1;
RO.add(Q, {rel_kad: 3, rel_sr: 1});
!}

The majority is pleased. The Internationalists issued a statement of regret, and some of their younger members are looking at Lenin's paper.

@intl
on-arrival: {!
RO.fac(Q, 'intl', 5, -6);
RO.fac(Q, 'defencist', -3, 4);
RO.fac(Q, 'rightdef', -2, 6);
Q.war_line -= 1;
RO.add(Q, {rel_kad: -3, rel_lsr: 2, rel_bol: 2});
!}

Martov's wing is happy. Potresov's wing is not, and has begun to write letters to the newspapers.

@balance
on-arrival: {!
RO.fac(Q, 'defencist', 0, -3);
RO.fac(Q, 'intl', 0, -4);
RO.fac(Q, 'rightdef', 0, -2);
!}

A carefully worded resolution satisfied nobody and offended nobody. For now.
